<title>FRANCE: U.S. tops Paris Jan-Feb air cargo export destination.</title>
<headline>U.S. tops Paris Jan-Feb air cargo export destination.</headline>
<text>
<p>PARIS, April 10 (Reuter)   The United States was the main</p>
<p>destination for export traffic handled at the Paris airports in January-February 1997, airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 leading destinations  by country for ADP exports(in tonnes) in January-February 1997, with percentage change on the same period last year, in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p>1.   United States				18,339     up     8.1</p>
<p>pct</p>
<p>2.   Japan					   4,785   down    17.5</p>
<p>3.   Germany					 3,674     up    26.8</p>
<p>4.   Hong Kong				     3,133   down     1.3</p>
<p>5.   UK						2,995     up    34.0</p>
<p>6.   Canada					  2,961   down    15.7</p>
<p>7.   Brazil					  2,701     up    45.6</p>
<p>8.   United Arab Emirates			2,374     up    23.5</p>
<p>9.   Mexico					  2,003     up     7.9</p>
<p>10.  India					   1,889   down    21.7</p>
<p>11.  French West Indies			  1,864   down     6.0</p>
<p>12.  Singapore				     1,750     up    46.5</p>
<p>13.  Saudi Arabia				  1,502   down     4.0</p>
<p>14.  Thailand					1,392     up    24.6</p>
<p>15.  Korea					   1,274     up     1.5</p>
<p>16.  Egypt					   1,250   down     7.8</p>
<p>17.  Italy					   1,219   down    16.2</p>
<p>18.  Lebanon					 1,029     up     2.1</p>
<p>19.  China					     987   down     9.6</p>
<p>20 . Senegal					   815     up    86.2</p>
<p>    Total    57,936  tonnes</p>
<p>Overall air cargo exports from Orly and CDG in January-February were 86,579 tonnes up 1.4 percent on the same period last year the airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
